(59553, 1501, 472, '<td valign="top">you get an A for effort!!!!</td>', 'you get an A for effort!!!!', '2002-05-13 08:10:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(59554, 1501, 1209, '<td valign="top">Thank you to all who took the time to look at, and vote for, my photo. This was my first entry, and it was done for two reasons: (1) to surprise my photographer daughter, "Digiteyes",  who LOVES this site! You need to check out her pics!   And, (2) to create an "ad" that showcased my other talented daughter''s creations, custon knit caps!    The picture worked on both counts.<br/>It''s been an adventure!  I was disqualified and the picture removed almost immediately, because the lettering looked photoshopped.  For all those who asked:<br/>Yes, the cap is real.<br/>Yes, the lettering on it is knitted into the cap.<br/>This cap was given to my daughter who lives and breathes dpchallange!<br/>Yes, more can be knit.<br/>No, Drew hasn''t yet given permission to use the dpchallenge logo, although he, too, has asked for a cap.<br/>Yes, the URL is real!<br/>No, if I remove the URL, how can the ad work?<br/>Yes, I know the URL is vertical; it got your attention didn''t it?<br/>Yes, Moondoggie, that is a Monte Vista Monarchs cap. My daughter knit dozens for their school to sell for a fundraiser.<br/>And, for all the others who didn''t notice the URL and asked about the caps,  go to www.fishknits.com<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thank you to all who took the time to look at, and vote for, my photo. This was my first entry, and it was done for two reasons: (1) to surprise my photographer daughter, "Digiteyes",  who LOVES this site! You need to check out her pics!   And, (2) to create an "ad" that showcased my other talented daughter''s creations, custon knit caps!    The picture worked on both counts.It''s been an adventure!  I was disqualified and the picture removed almost immediately, because the lettering looked photoshopped.  For all those who asked:Yes, the cap is real.Yes, the lettering on it is knitted into the cap.This cap was given to my daughter who lives and breathes dpchallange!Yes, more can be knit.No, Drew hasn''t yet given permission to use the dpchallenge logo, although he, too, has asked for a cap.Yes, the URL is real!No, if I remove the URL, how can the ad work?Yes, I know the URL is vertical; it got your attention didn''t it?Yes, Moondoggie, that is a Monte Vista Monarchs cap. My daughter knit dozens for their school to sell for a fundraiser.And, for all the others who didn''t notice the URL and asked about the caps,  go to www.fishknits.com ', '2002-05-13 13:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
